{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1256160-bizarrest-character-s-you-ever-made","id":1256160,"title":"Bizarrest Character's you ever made","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-21T10:51:35-07:00","id":1256160,"title":"Bizarrest Character's you ever made","content":"Im currently making a character for a VtM game where im playing as....<br /> <br /> Elvis Presley.<br /> Basically he got tired of being famous and decided to lay low for a while. Hiring an Impersonator as the real Elvis traveled through america trying to pass for an Impersonator. Then the real impersonator passed away, He was found by his sire (Janis Joplin) who embraced him to keep his legacy alive. <br /> Currently Elvis recides in Las Vegas. Guilt Ridden for knowing that he wont ever be able to get close to his family again. Knowing he lives under the shadow of his former fame, Running a school for impersonators and working in the local wedding chapel. Elvis Lives as a Daughter of Cacophony, Sorrowful as The Nowhere King...Waiting for his moment to shine once more.<br /> <br /> Hail to the King, Babeh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T15:53:16-07:00","id":1256566,"title":"","content":"Once I played a Tzimisce who flesh-crafted himself to look exactly like Kanye West. Just because he wanted to. No particular reason. Then he forgot how to use Vicissitude after a traumatic experience, and now is stuck looking exactly like Kanye for the rest of his unlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T01:49:36-07:00","id":1256662,"title":"","content":"The trouble with using famous real people as your characters is that almost all players simply aren't up to roleplaying as that famous person. So these sort of 'rip-off' characters always end up as a joke (especially for the other players if the owner is trying to be serious), a weak pastiche, or at worst just mockery. Being inspired by famous people is cool but you have to be original and create your own character instead of trying to steal the limelight from your idol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T03:51:40-07:00","id":1256681,"title":"","content":"A jaded Toreador elder who was the model for Michelangelo's David. His sire's rival was the Toreador patron of Michelangelo himself, and she tried to one-up her rival by embracing the model, so that she'd have her own 'David.' Unfortunately, he turned out to be a vapid pretty-boy, and she tired of him quickly. He definitely 'peaked too early,' in that he had little artistic vision of his own (although he mastered several artistic disciplines over the centuries), and was only ever famous for being 'that guy they made a statue of.'<br /> <br /> He's old, powerful, connected to the hilt, and *everybody* in Clan Toreador knows that he's pretty much a mistake-done-good, only having achieved what elder status he has by dint of not dying or screwing up badly over the last 400-plus years, being pretty much the definition of 'playing it safe.'<br /> <br /> His name is *not* David, and he's long past being annoyed by people calling him David, since that joke got old a long time ago. He's well aware of how the rest of the Clan regards him, and considers their disdain amusing, since he's managed to get by without their respect, and puts on a good show of not caring...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","user":"Ian Turner","date":". 09-23-2018, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T04:44:58-07:00","id":1256689,"title":"","content":"Not mine, but I drag this one out on occasion.<br /> <br /> No shit, there I was... this was in spring '98 or '99, I think. I was running a LARP at a small local convention in deep rural southwest Kentucky. There I was, minding my own business at the registration and logistics desk, when a pack of my prospective players staggered into the room in what was either a Fleshcrafted gamer-centipede mass or a consensual close-order formation of mutual support for upright locomotion. It was just past three in the afternoon and I could smell the liquor and questionable decisions from across the room.<br /> <br /> &quot;Heeeeey,&quot; one slurred, fumbling in his pin-festooned leather vest for what I hoped was not a weapon. &quot;I heard yer runnin' a Vamfire game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Trepidatiously, I responded in the affirmative.<br /> <br /> &quot;Awesome.&quot; He located the object of his search and withdrew, to my rmingled relief and slowly-rising dread, a small wad of paper. As he unfolded it like some non-Euclidean eldritch origami horror, I recognized it as a character sheet. It appeared to have been used as a placemat for last night's pizza and this morning's coffee, and under the layers of organic debris, the owner's pen had left no dot behind. &quot;I wanna bring in my home chara... chiro... character. I call 'im 'Roadkill.' He's a <b>Samedi wererabbit Abomination</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T06:41:54-07:00","id":1256702,"title":"","content":"Uhm.... some time ago, I made a character named Aleister Crowley, only son of a british hippy couple, that had decided to give him that name to show how they were unaffected by moral standards of the society.<br /> But actually the kid developed in a man that become an architect and civil designer that didn't wanted anything to do with of that sh*t. I also took a flaw like &quot;unlucky&quot;.or something similar, I don't remember that well.<br /> I just wanted to give him some social awkardness, not really great hardships.<br /> I then left all to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> Flashforward, Aleister got Embraced by a dumb Caitiff thinking he was some kind of dark overlord and couldn't restrain himself while &quot;testing&quot; the overlord...<br /> Aleister then developed Obtenebration, Auspex and a original Discipline that was the one-path version of some Thaumaturgy Path that had something to do with summoning, I don't remember which...<br /> <br /> Flashforward. Several months later Aleister is &quot;prisoner&quot; of his sire that threaten him and thinks he bloodbounded him (luckily I had taken the merit &quot;unboundable&quot;) and so one night he offs his sire w\u00ecth the old trick of &quot;Surprise! Stake &amp; Sun!&quot;<br /> <br /> Flashforward. All the Kindred around misinterpreted in the worst possible way and think he some big demonic offshot. Soon he gets ambushed by a couple of Archons and survive (they both get out of it, in Torpor, and Aleister just store them in some garage because he didn't had real issue with them), therefore his legend widens.<br /> <br /> Flashforward. Soon, the Camarilla starts actively hunting him, and after the poor guy survives all by sheer luck, he is added to the Red List out of a misunderstanding thanks to the poor choice of his parents in naming him.<br /> <br /> Last time anyone did see him, he had stumbled in an ambush or Alastors and Josians and was rescued at the last moment by a rag-tag assault by a coterie of members of the Red List.<br /> And one of them says to this poor Humanity 7 guy, &quot;so, do you want to join us and tear the world to pieces?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The End.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T09:38:58-07:00","id":1256735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tegyrius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1256160-bizarrest-character-s-you-ever-made?p=1256689#post1256689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;I wanna bring in my home chara... chiro... character. I call 'im 'Roadkill.' He's a <b>Samedi wererabbit Abomination</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds completely believable for the time period. I say this because this was about the same period I would see people on AOL playing 4th generation Japanese Kiasyd who were 7 feet tall and wielding twin silver-coated Zambato (which are these things which look like oversized katana with 6 foot long blades, basically designed to cut the heads off of horses).<br /> <br /> I think my personal oddest character was a medieval Tzimisce elder who was constantly trying to replace the brains of humans with ghoul rats so that he could control them via Animalism. (Results were mixed. Subjects tended to chew on themselves and pee a lot when not beating their heads against the wall.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T13:47:36-07:00","id":1256788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1256160-bizarrest-character-s-you-ever-made?p=1256735#post1256735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Results were mixed. Subjects tended to chew on themselves and pee a lot when not beating their heads against the wall</div> </div> </div> </div>a total win, based on my experience with Tzimisce... :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes